Chapter 2 Motor Vehicle Registration

Section 1 Initial Registration

Article 10: Where applying for a motor vehicle license plate and vehicle license for the first time, the motor vehicle owner shall apply for initial registration with the vehicle administration office at the place of residence.

Article 11: The motor vehicle owner shall have the motor vehicle undergo a safety technical inspection at a motor vehicle safety technical inspection institution, obtain a motor vehicle safety technical inspection certificate of conformity, and then apply for initial registration. However, motor vehicles imported through customs and motor vehicles determined by the competent department for motor vehicle products under the State Council to be exempt from safety technical inspection shall be exempted.

Motor vehicles exempt from safety technical inspection that fall under any of the following circumstances shall undergo a safety technical inspection:
(1) Domestically produced motor vehicles that have not applied for initial registration within two years after leaving the factory;
(2) Motor vehicles imported through customs that have not applied for initial registration within two years after importation;
(3) Traffic accidents occurring before applying for initial registration.

Before applying for initial registration, special school buses shall undergo a safety technical inspection in accordance with the national safety technical standards for special school buses.

Article 12: Where applying for initial registration, the motor vehicle owner shall present the motor vehicle for inspection, confirm the application information, and submit the following certificates and vouchers:
(1) Identity certificate of the motor vehicle owner;
(2) Vehicle purchase invoice or other certificate of origin of the motor vehicle;
(3) Certificate of conformity for the complete motor vehicle leaving the factory or import voucher for imported motor vehicles;
(4) Certificate of compulsory traffic accident liability insurance for motor vehicles;
(5) Tax payment certificate or tax exemption certificate for vehicle purchase tax and vessel and vehicle tax, except where laws provide that they are not within the scope of taxation;
(6) Other certificates and vouchers required to be submitted at the time of motor vehicle initial registration as provided by laws and administrative regulations.

Motor vehicles other than those imported through customs and those determined by the competent department for motor vehicle products under the State Council to be exempt from safety technical inspection shall also submit a motor vehicle safety technical inspection certificate of conformity.

The vehicle administration office shall, within two days from the date of accepting the application, inspect the motor vehicle, collect and verify the vehicle identification number rubbing or electronic data, examine the submitted certificates and vouchers, and issue the motor vehicle registration certificate, license plate, vehicle license, and inspection qualification mark.

Where information on motor vehicle safety technical inspection, taxation, insurance, etc., is networked for verification with relevant departments or institutions, the applicant shall be exempt from submitting relevant certificates and vouchers, and the vehicle administration office shall verify the relevant electronic information.

Article 13: When handling initial registration for fire trucks, ambulances, and engineering rescue vehicles, the vehicle administration office shall examine the vehicle's usage nature, marking patterns, marking lights, and alarms.

Where the motor vehicle owner applies to register the usage nature of the motor vehicle as hazardous goods transportation, road passenger transport, or tourist passenger transport, they shall possess the relevant road transport permit. Where road transport permit information and vehicle usage nature information are networked for verification with relevant departments, the vehicle administration office shall verify the relevant electronic information.

Where applying to register a hazardous goods transport vehicle, the motor vehicle owner shall be a unit.

When handling initial registration, the vehicle administration office shall separately issue the motor vehicle registration certificate, license plate, vehicle license, and inspection qualification mark for the tractor and the trailer.

Article 14: Where the vehicle administration office is networked with new vehicle factory inspection information from motor vehicle manufacturers, the motor vehicle owner applying for initial registration of small and micro non-commercial passenger cars shall be exempt from presenting the motor vehicle for inspection.

The vehicle administration office shall, together with relevant departments, promote the sale of motor vehicles with license plates at qualified motorcycle sales enterprises, facilitating motor vehicle owners to handle vehicle purchase, insurance purchase, tax payment, and initial registration in a one-stop manner.

Article 15: Initial registration shall not be handled under any of the following circumstances:
(1) The certificates and vouchers submitted by the motor vehicle owner are invalid;
(2) The certificate of origin of the motor vehicle has been altered, or the motor vehicle owner recorded in the certificate of origin does not match the identity certificate;
(3) The certificates and vouchers submitted by the motor vehicle owner do not match the motor vehicle;
(4) The motor vehicle is produced without permission from the competent department for motor vehicle products under the State Council or imported without permission from the national competent department for imported motor vehicles;
(5) The model or relevant technical parameters of the motor vehicle do not conform to the announcement of the competent department for motor vehicle products under the State Council;
(6) The vehicle identification number or relevant technical parameters of the motor vehicle do not conform to national safety technical standards;
(7) The motor vehicle has reached the national mandatory scrapping standard;
(8) The motor vehicle has been lawfully seized or detained by supervisory organs, people's courts, people's procuratorates, or administrative law enforcement departments;
(9) The motor vehicle is stolen, robbed, or defrauded;
(10) Other circumstances not in conformity with laws and administrative regulations.

Section 2 Change Registration

Article 16: Where a registered motor vehicle falls under any of the following circumstances, the motor vehicle owner shall apply for change registration with the vehicle administration office at the place of registration:
(1) Changing the body color;
(2) Replacing the engine;
(3) Replacing the body or frame;
(4) Replacing the complete vehicle due to quality issues;
(5) The registered usage nature of the motor vehicle changes;
(6) The domicile of the motor vehicle owner moves out of or into the jurisdiction of the vehicle administration office.

Where the change matters fall under items 1 to 3 of the first paragraph, the motor vehicle owner shall apply for change registration with the vehicle administration office within ten days after the change.

Article 17: Where applying for change registration, the motor vehicle owner shall present the motor vehicle for inspection, confirm the application information, and submit the following certificates and vouchers:
(1) Identity certificate of the motor vehicle owner;
(2) Motor vehicle registration certificate;
(3) Motor vehicle vehicle license;
(4) Where replacing the engine, body, or frame, a motor vehicle safety technical inspection certificate of conformity shall also be submitted;
(5) Where replacing the complete vehicle due to quality issues, also

within ten days, apply to the vehicle management office at the place of registration for change filing:
(1) where the domicile of the motor vehicle owner moves within the jurisdiction of the vehicle management office, or the name (unit name) of the motor vehicle owner changes;
(2) where the name or number of the identity document of the motor vehicle owner changes;
(3) where the contact information of the motor vehicle owner changes;
(4) where the vehicle identification number is illegible or damaged due to wear, rust, accident, or other reasons;
(5) where a limb disability operating auxiliary device is installed, removed, or replaced on a small or micro automatic passenger car;
(6) where a vehicle-mounted crane tailgate is installed or removed on a truck or trailer;
(7) where a roof luggage rack is installed on a small or micro passenger car without changing the main body structure of the vehicle body and ensuring safety, and where different styles of radiator grilles, bumpers, or wheel hubs are replaced; where wheel hubs are replaced, the tire specifications shall not be changed.
Article 24: Where applying for change filing, the motor vehicle owner shall confirm the application information and handle it in accordance with the following provisions:
(1) where it falls under the circumstances prescribed in Item 1 of Article 23, the motor vehicle owner shall submit the identity document, motor vehicle registration certificate, and driving license; the vehicle management office shall, within one day from the date of acceptance, endorse the filing matters on the motor vehicle registration certificate, take back and reissue the driving license;
(2) where it falls under the circumstances prescribed in Item 2 of Article 23, the motor vehicle owner shall submit the identity document and motor vehicle registration certificate; where the number of the identity document changes, the relevant change certificate shall also be submitted; the vehicle management office shall, within one day from the date of acceptance, endorse the filing matters on the motor vehicle registration certificate;
(3) where it falls under the circumstances prescribed in Item 3 of Article 23, the motor vehicle owner shall submit the identity document; the vehicle management office shall complete the filing within one day from the date of acceptance;
(4) where it falls under the circumstances prescribed in Item 4 of Article 23, the motor vehicle owner shall submit the identity document, motor vehicle registration certificate, and driving license, and present the motor vehicle for inspection; the vehicle management office shall, within one day from the date of acceptance, inspect the motor vehicle, supervise the re-stamping of the original vehicle identification number, collect and verify the vehicle identification number rubbing film or electronic data, and endorse the filing matters on the motor vehicle registration certificate;
(5) where it falls under the circumstances prescribed in Items 5 and 6 of Article 23, the motor vehicle owner shall submit the identity document, driving license, motor vehicle safety technical inspection certificate, and certificate of qualified installation of the operating auxiliary device or tailgate, and present the motor vehicle for inspection; the vehicle management office shall, within one day from the date of acceptance, inspect the motor vehicle, take back and reissue the driving license;
(6) where it falls under the circumstances prescribed in Item 7 of Article 23, the motor vehicle owner shall submit the identity document and driving license, and present the motor vehicle for inspection; the vehicle management office shall, within one day from the date of acceptance, inspect the motor vehicle, take back and reissue the driving license.
Where applying for change filing under Items 5, 6, and 7 of Article 23 and the vehicle is not at the place of registration, an application may be submitted to the vehicle management office at the place where the vehicle is located. The vehicle management office at the place where the vehicle is located shall inspect the motor vehicle in accordance with regulations, examine the submitted certificates and vouchers, and transfer the electronic data of the motor vehicle inspection to the vehicle management office at the place of registration; the vehicle management office at the place of registration shall review and re-examine in accordance with regulations and issue the driving license.
Section 3 Transfer Registration
Article 25: Where the ownership of a registered motor vehicle is transferred, the current motor vehicle owner shall apply to the vehicle management office at the place of registration for transfer registration within thirty days from the date of delivery of the motor vehicle.
Before applying for transfer registration, the motor vehicle owner shall complete the handling of road traffic safety violations and traffic accidents involving the vehicle.
Article 26: Where applying for transfer registration, the current motor vehicle owner shall present the motor vehicle for inspection, confirm the application information, and submit the following certificates and vouchers:
(1) the identity document of the current motor vehicle owner;
(2) the certificate and voucher for the transfer of motor vehicle ownership;
(3) the motor vehicle registration certificate;
(4) the motor vehicle driving license;
(5) where the motor vehicle is under customs supervision, the certificate of release from customs supervision of the supervised vehicle or the transfer certificate approved by the customs shall also be submitted;
(6) where the motor vehicle has exceeded the inspection validity period, the motor vehicle safety technical inspection certificate and the traffic accident liability compulsory insurance certificate shall also be submitted.
The vehicle management office shall, within one day from the date of accepting the application, inspect the motor vehicle, verify the vehicle identification number rubbing film or electronic data, examine the submitted certificates and vouchers, take back the license plate and driving license, determine the new motor vehicle license plate number, endorse the transfer matters on the motor vehicle registration certificate, and reissue the license plate, driving license, and inspection qualification mark.
Where applying for transfer registration during the period of motor vehicle mortgage registration, it shall be jointly applied for by the original motor vehicle owner, the current motor vehicle owner, and the mortgagee, and the vehicle management office shall handle the new mortgage registration together.
Where applying for transfer registration during the period of motor vehicle pledge filing, it shall be jointly applied for by the original motor vehicle owner, the current motor vehicle owner, and the pledgee, and the vehicle management office shall handle the new pledge filing together.
Article 27: When the vehicle management office handles transfer registration, if the domicile of the current motor vehicle owner is not within the jurisdiction of the vehicle management office, the vehicle management office at the place of transfer-out shall, within three days from the date of acceptance, inspect the motor vehicle, verify the vehicle identification number rubbing film or electronic data, examine the submitted certificates and vouchers, take back the license plate and driving license, endorse the transfer and change matters on the motor vehicle registration certificate, issue a temporary driving vehicle license plate valid for thirty days, and create and upload the motor vehicle electronic archive data. The motor vehicle owner shall apply to the vehicle management office at the place of transfer-in for motor vehicle transfer-in within the validity period of the temporary driving vehicle license plate.
When applying for motor vehicle transfer-in, the motor vehicle owner shall confirm the application information, submit the identity document, motor vehicle registration certificate

