(2) The motor vehicle has not reached the national mandatory scrapping standard, and the motor vehicle owner voluntarily scraps it;
(3) The motor vehicle is lost due to natural disasters, fire, traffic accidents, etc.;
(4) The motor vehicle is not used within the territory of China for some reason;
(5) The vehicle is returned due to quality issues.

Where the circumstances specified in Item 4 or Item 5 of the first paragraph apply, before the motor vehicle owner applies for cancellation of registration, the road traffic safety violations and traffic accidents involving the vehicle shall be handled.

Where the circumstances specified in Item 4 of the first paragraph apply to the export of used cars, the used car export enterprise shall apply for cancellation of registration within two months after the motor vehicle completes customs export clearance procedures.

Article 38 Where the circumstances specified in Item 1 or Item 2 of the first paragraph of Article 37 apply, and the motor vehicle owner applies for cancellation of registration, the motor vehicle shall be sold to a scrap motor vehicle recycling enterprise, the application information shall be confirmed, and the motor vehicle registration certificate, license plate, and driving license shall be submitted.

The scrap motor vehicle recycling enterprise shall confirm the motor vehicle, issue a scrap motor vehicle recycling certificate to the motor vehicle owner, and submit the application form, motor vehicle registration certificate, license plate, driving license, and a copy of the scrap motor vehicle recycling certificate to the vehicle management office within seven days. Where it is a scrapped school bus, large passenger bus, heavy truck, or other operating vehicle, when applying for cancellation of registration, the vehicle identification number rubbing film, photos or electronic data of vehicle dismantling shall also be submitted.

The vehicle management office shall, within one day from the date of acceptance, review the submitted certificates and vouchers, recover the motor vehicle registration certificate, license plate, and driving license, and issue a cancellation certificate.

Where the vehicle is not at the place of registration, the motor vehicle owner may sell the scrap motor vehicle to a motor vehicle recycling enterprise at the place where the vehicle is located. The scrap motor vehicle recycling enterprise shall confirm the motor vehicle, issue a scrap motor vehicle recycling certificate to the motor vehicle owner, and submit the application form, motor vehicle registration certificate, license plate, driving license, copy of the scrap motor vehicle recycling certificate, and vehicle identification number rubbing film or electronic data to the vehicle management office at the place of scrapping within seven days. Where it is a scrapped school bus, large passenger bus, heavy truck, or other operating vehicle, photos or electronic data of vehicle dismantling shall also be submitted.

The vehicle management office at the place of scrapping shall, within one day from the date of acceptance, review the submitted certificates and vouchers, recover the motor vehicle registration certificate, license plate, and driving license, and transmit the motor vehicle scrapping information to the vehicle management office at the place of registration through the computer registration management system. The vehicle management office at the place of registration shall complete the cancellation registration within one day from the date of receiving the motor vehicle scrapping information, and issue a cancellation certificate.

Where motor vehicle scrapping information is networked for verification with relevant departments, the scrap motor vehicle recycling enterprise shall be exempted from submitting relevant certificates and vouchers, and the vehicle management office shall verify the relevant electronic information.

Article 39 Where the circumstances specified in Item 3, Item 4, or Item 5 of the first paragraph of Article 37 apply, and the motor vehicle owner applies for cancellation of registration, the application information shall be confirmed, and the following certificates and vouchers shall be submitted:
(1) Identity certificate of the motor vehicle owner;
(2) Motor vehicle registration certificate;
(3) Motor vehicle driving license;
(4) Where the motor vehicle is under customs supervision and is not used within the territory of China for some reason, the Notice of Entry/Exit and Plate Issuance/Cancellation for Customs-Supervised Vehicles issued by the customs shall also be submitted;
(5) Where the vehicle is returned due to quality issues, a vehicle return certificate issued by the motor vehicle manufacturer or dealer shall also be submitted.

Where an applicant handles cancellation of registration due to the loss of the motor vehicle, they shall make a written commitment that the motor vehicle was lost due to natural disasters, fire, traffic accidents, etc., and bear legal responsibility for false commitments.

Where a used car export enterprise handles cancellation of registration due to used car export, it shall submit the identity certificate of the motor vehicle owner, the motor vehicle registration certificate, and the motor vehicle export certificate.

The vehicle management office shall, within one day from the date of acceptance, review the submitted certificates and vouchers. Where the motor vehicle is not used within the territory of China for some reason, the motor vehicle exit record shall also be verified. The motor vehicle registration certificate, license plate, and driving license shall be recovered, and a cancellation certificate shall be issued.

Article 40 Where a registered motor vehicle falls under any of the following circumstances, the vehicle management office at the place of registration shall handle the cancellation of the motor vehicle:
(1) The motor vehicle registration is revoked according to law;
(2) A motor vehicle that has reached the national mandatory scrapping standard is lawfully seized and forcibly scrapped.

Article 41 Where a registered motor vehicle falls under any of the following circumstances, the vehicle management office shall announce that the motor vehicle registration certificate, license plate, and driving license are invalid:
(1) The motor vehicle has reached the national mandatory scrapping standard, and the motor vehicle owner fails to handle cancellation of registration within the time limit;
(2) After the motor vehicle registration is revoked according to law, the motor vehicle registration certificate, license plate, and driving license are not recovered;
(3) A motor vehicle that has reached the national mandatory scrapping standard is lawfully seized and forcibly scrapped;
(4) The motor vehicle owner fails to return the motor vehicle registration certificate, license plate, and driving license when handling cancellation of registration.

Article 42 Where the circumstances specified in Item 1, Item 8, or Item 9 of Article 15, or Item 1 of Article 29 apply, cancellation of registration shall not be handled. During the period of mortgage registration or pledge filing of a motor vehicle, cancellation of registration shall not be handled.

Chapter 3 Motor Vehicle License Plates and Certificates
Section 1 Issuance of License Plates and Certificates
Article 43 The motor vehicle owner may determine the motor vehicle license plate number by randomly selecting it through a computer or by arranging it themselves according to the number selection rules.

The public security organ traffic management department shall use a unified motor vehicle license plate number selection system to issue license plate numbers, and license plate numbers shall be issued publicly to the society.

Article 44 After handling motor vehicle change registration, transfer registration, or cancellation registration, when the original motor vehicle owner applies for motor vehicle registration, they may apply to the vehicle management office to use the original motor vehicle license plate number.

The application to use the original motor vehicle license plate number shall comply with

The following conditions:
(1) An application is made within two years after handling the deregistration of a motor vehicle, change of co-owners, transfer registration, or cancellation registration;
(2) The motor vehicle owner has owned the original motor vehicle and used the original license plate number for more than one year;
(3) Road traffic safety violations and traffic accidents involving the original motor vehicle have been fully resolved.
Article 45 Where the registered owner's name of a motor vehicle jointly owned by a married couple is changed to the name of the other party, and the marital relationship has lasted for one year and both spouses jointly apply, the original motor vehicle license plate number may be used.
Article 46 Where a motor vehicle falls under any of the following circumstances and needs to temporarily travel on the road, the motor vehicle owner shall apply to the vehicle administration office for a temporary vehicle license plate:
(1) Not yet sold;
(2) Not yet registered after obtaining the motor vehicle through purchase, allocation, gift, or other means;
(3) New vehicles exported for sale;
(4) Conducting scientific research or type approval tests;
(5) Special-purpose motor vehicles that are not registered due to axle load, total mass, or overall dimensions exceeding national standards.
Article 47 A motor vehicle owner applying for a temporary vehicle license plate shall submit the following documents and vouchers:
(1) Identity proof of the motor vehicle owner;
(2) Certificate of compulsory traffic accident liability insurance for motor vehicles;
(3) Where the circumstances specified in Article 46, Item (1) or Item (5) apply, the motor vehicle whole vehicle factory certificate of conformity or import certificate for imported motor vehicles shall also be submitted;
(4) Where the circumstances specified in Article 46, Item (2) apply, proof of the origin of the motor vehicle, as well as the motor vehicle whole vehicle factory certificate of conformity or import certificate for imported motor vehicles, shall also be submitted;
(5) Where the circumstances specified in Article 46, Item (3) apply, the safety technical inspection certificate issued by the motor vehicle manufacturer and the motor vehicle export certificate shall also be submitted;
(6) Where the circumstances specified in Article 46, Item (4) apply, a written application, as well as the motor vehicle safety technical inspection certificate of conformity or the safety technical inspection certificate issued by the motor vehicle manufacturer, shall also be submitted.
The vehicle administration office shall, within one day from the date of acceptance, review the submitted documents and vouchers. Where the circumstances specified in Article 46, Item (1), Item (2), or Item (3) apply and temporary travel on the road is required, a temporary vehicle license plate with a validity period not exceeding thirty days shall be issued. Where the circumstances specified in Article 46, Item (4) apply, a temporary vehicle license plate with a validity period not exceeding six months shall be issued. Where the circumstances specified in Article 46, Item (5) apply, a temporary vehicle license plate with a validity period not exceeding ninety days shall be issued.
Where license plates cannot be issued within the prescribed time limit due to reasons related to license plate production, the vehicle administration office shall issue a temporary vehicle license plate with a validity period not exceeding fifteen days.
For circumstances specified in Article 46, Item (1) or Item (2), where the motor vehicle owner needs to apply for a temporary vehicle license plate multiple times, the vehicle administration office shall not issue a temporary vehicle license plate more than three times. For circumstances specified in Article 46, Item (3), the vehicle administration office shall issue a temporary vehicle license plate only once.
The validity period of a temporary vehicle license plate shall not exceed the validity period of the compulsory traffic accident liability insurance for motor vehicles.
After a motor vehicle is registered, the temporary vehicle license plate shall become invalid three days after the motor vehicle owner receives the motor vehicle license plate and shall not continue to be used.
Article 48 Where road testing or demonstration application of intelligent connected motor vehicles requires travel on the road, the road testing or demonstration application unit shall apply to the vehicle administration office for a temporary vehicle license plate and submit the following documents and vouchers:
(1) Identity proof of the road testing or demonstration application unit;
(2) Certificate of compulsory traffic accident liability insurance for motor vehicles;
(3) Road testing or demonstration application certificate confirmed by the competent department;
(4) Motor vehicle safety technical inspection certificate of conformity.
The vehicle administration office shall, within one day from the date of acceptance, review the submitted documents and vouchers and issue a temporary vehicle license plate. The validity period of the temporary vehicle license plate shall be consistent with the period endorsed on the road testing or demonstration application certificate, but shall not exceed six months at most.
Article 49 Where a temporarily imported motor vehicle needs to travel on the road, the motor vehicle owner shall apply to the vehicle administration office at the place of entry or the place of departure in accordance with regulations for a temporary entry motor vehicle license plate and driving license.
Article 50 The public security organ traffic management department shall use a unified license plate management information system to produce, issue, recover, and destroy motor vehicle license plates and temporary vehicle license plates.
Section 2 Replacement and Reissuance of License Plates and Certificates
Article 51 Where a motor vehicle license plate is lost, missing, or damaged, the motor vehicle owner shall apply to the vehicle administration office at the place of registration for reissuance or replacement. Upon application, the motor vehicle owner shall confirm the application information and submit identity proof.
The vehicle administration office shall review the submitted documents and vouchers, recover any license plate that has not been lost, missing, or damaged, and reissue or replace the license plate within fifteen days from the date of acceptance, with the original motor vehicle license plate number unchanged.
During the period of reissuance or replacement of the license plate, the applicant may apply for a temporary vehicle license plate with a validity period not exceeding fifteen days.
Upon reissuance or replacement of a motor vehicle license plate, the original motor vehicle license plate shall become invalid and shall not continue to be used.
Article 52 Where a motor vehicle registration certificate or driving license is lost, missing, or damaged, the motor vehicle owner shall apply to the vehicle administration office at the place of registration for reissuance or replacement. Upon application, the motor vehicle owner shall confirm the application information and submit identity proof.
The vehicle administration office shall review the submitted documents and vouchers, recover the damaged registration certificate or driving license, and reissue or replace the registration certificate or driving license within one day from the date of acceptance.
Upon reissuance or replacement of a motor vehicle registration certificate or driving license, the original motor vehicle registration certificate or driving license shall become invalid and shall not continue to be used.
