Pursue criminal liability against relevant responsible persons.
Article 73 Personnel engaged in motor vehicle inspection work shall hold qualification certificates issued by the public security organ traffic management department. The public security organ traffic management department shall select a sufficient number of motor vehicle inspectors from among public security police officers and auxiliary police personnel to engage in inspection work. Staff of motor vehicle registration service stations may undertake motor vehicle inspection work under the supervision of the vehicle management office.

Motor vehicle inspectors shall strictly observe work discipline for inspections, shall not reduce inspection items or lower inspection standards, and shall not participate in, assist, or condone the handling of registration for non-compliant motor vehicles. Public security police officers and auxiliary police personnel shall not participate in or indirectly participate in the business activities of motor vehicle safety technical inspection institutions, and shall not accept money or property from motor vehicle safety technical inspection institutions, motor vehicle sales enterprises, second-hand vehicle trading markets, scrap motor vehicle recycling enterprises, and other relevant enterprises or applicants.

The vehicle management office shall conduct full-process video recording of the motor vehicle inspection process and monitor the inspection process in real time; where video recording equipment is not used, no inspection shall be conducted. During motor vehicle inspection, the inspector shall use a duty law enforcement recorder to record the inspection process. The vehicle management office shall establish audio-visual archives of motor vehicle inspections and store the audio-visual materials recorded by video recording equipment and duty law enforcement recorders.

Article 74 Where, in the course of handling motor vehicle registration and related business, the vehicle management office discovers any of the following circumstances, it shall promptly carry out an investigation:
(1) The motor vehicle is suspected of smuggling, theft, robbery, fraud, illegal production or sale, assembly (combination) assembly, or illegal modification;
(2) It is suspected of submitting false application materials;
(3) It is suspected of using forged or altered motor vehicle license plates and certificates;
(4) It is suspected of obtaining motor vehicle registration by deception, bribery, or other improper means;
(5) There are abnormal circumstances such as frequent replacement of license plates and certificates, transfer registration, transfer-out and transfer-in within a short period;
(6) There are other illegal or non-compliant circumstances.

Where the vehicle management office discovers that an applicant handling motor vehicle registration and related business via the Internet has circumstances suspected as provided in the first paragraph, it shall convert the handling to on-site processing, examine the application materials on the spot, and promptly carry out an investigation.

Article 75 When carrying out an investigation, the vehicle management office may notify the applicant to assist in the investigation, inquire into the suspected circumstances, record the investigation content, and may use methods such as inspection and appraisal and on-site inspection for verification.

Where an investigation reveals involvement in an administrative case or a criminal case, necessary compulsory measures or other disposal measures shall be taken in accordance with the law, and the case shall be transferred to the public security organ with jurisdiction for handling in accordance with the "Provisions of Public Security Organs on Procedures for Handling Administrative Cases," the "Provisions of Public Security Organs on Procedures for Handling Criminal Cases," and other relevant provisions.

Where a motor vehicle is discovered to be suspected of smuggling during motor vehicle registration, the public security organ traffic management department shall transfer the motor vehicle and relevant materials to the customs for handling in accordance with the law.

Article 76 Where a registered motor vehicle is stolen, robbed, or defrauded, the vehicle management office shall, based on the situation provided by the criminal investigation department, record it in the computer registration system and stop handling all registration and business for that vehicle. After the stolen, robbed, or defrauded motor vehicle is returned, the vehicle management office shall resume handling all registration and business for that vehicle.

Where, during the period of being stolen, robbed, or defrauded, the engine number, vehicle identification number, or body color of a motor vehicle is changed, the vehicle management office shall handle the change filing based on the relevant technical appraisal certificate.

Article 77 The public security organ traffic management department and its traffic police and auxiliary police personnel handling motor vehicle registration work shall accept supervision lawfully implemented by supervisory organs, public security organ inspection and audit departments, etc.

The public security organ traffic management department and its traffic police and auxiliary police personnel handling motor vehicle registration work shall consciously accept supervision by society and citizens.

Chapter 6 Legal Liability

Article 78 Where any of the following circumstances exists, the public security organ traffic management department shall give a warning or impose a fine of not more than 200 yuan:
(1) The body or rear of the vehicle compartment of a heavy or medium-sized truck, special operation vehicle, trailer, or large passenger bus is not sprayed with an enlarged license plate number as prescribed, or the enlarged license plate number is unclear;
(2) A motor vehicle sprays or pastes logos or body advertisements that affect safe driving;
(3) A truck, special operation vehicle, or trailer is not equipped with side and rear lower protective devices as prescribed, or body reflective signs are not pasted;
(4) A motor vehicle does not undergo safety technical inspection within the prescribed time limit;
(5) The body color is changed, or the engine, body, or frame is replaced, and change registration is not handled within the time limit prescribed in Article 16;
(6) After the transfer of motor vehicle ownership, the current motor vehicle owner does not handle transfer registration within the time limit prescribed in Article 25;
(7) The motor vehicle owner handling change registration or transfer registration does not apply to the vehicle management office at the place of domicile for transfer-in of the motor vehicle within the time limit prescribed in Articles 18 and 27;
(8) The motor vehicle owner does not apply for change filing as prescribed in Article 23.

Article 79 Except for the circumstances prescribed in Articles 16, 22, and 23, where the appearance of a motor vehicle and the relevant technical parameters already registered are changed without authorization, the public security organ traffic management department shall order restoration to the original condition and impose a warning or a fine of not more than 500 yuan.

Article 80 Where relevant circumstances are concealed or false materials are provided to apply for motor vehicle registration, the public security organ traffic management department shall not accept or shall not register the application, and shall impose a fine of not more than 500 yuan; the applicant shall not apply for motor vehicle registration again within one year.

Where it is discovered that an applicant seeks improper benefits in motor vehicle registration business through means such as false motor vehicle transactions or using legal forms to conceal illegal purposes, the provisions of the first paragraph shall apply.

Article 81 Where motor vehicle registration is obtained by deception, bribery, or other improper means, the public security organ traffic management department shall...

collect the motor vehicle registration certificate, license plate, and vehicle license, revoke the motor vehicle registration, and impose a fine of not more than 2,000 yuan; the applicant shall not apply for motor vehicle registration again within three years.
Where supplementary or replacement services for motor vehicle registration certificates, license plates, vehicle licenses, and inspection qualification marks are handled by fraud, bribery, or other improper means, the public security organ traffic management department shall collect the motor vehicle registration certificate, license plate, vehicle license, and inspection qualification mark; if not collected, they shall be announced as invalid, and a fine of not more than 2,000 yuan shall be imposed.
Where any person organizes or participates in implementing any of the acts listed in Article 80 or the preceding two paragraphs of this Article to obtain economic benefits, the public security organ traffic management department shall impose a fine of not less than three times but not more than five times the illegal income, but the maximum shall not exceed 100,000 yuan.
Article 82 The public security departments of provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government may, according to the actual conditions of their respective regions and within the scope of the penalty range prescribed in these Provisions, formulate specific implementation standards.
The handling procedures for road traffic safety violations under these Provisions shall be implemented in accordance with the "Provisions on the Handling Procedures for Road Traffic Safety Violations."
Article 83 Traffic police who have any of the following circumstances shall be given sanctions in accordance with relevant regulations; employed personnel shall be dismissed; if a crime is constituted, criminal responsibility shall be investigated according to law:
(1) Handling registration for motor vehicles that are stolen, robbed, defrauded, smuggled, illegally assembled (combined), or have reached the national mandatory scrapping standards in violation of regulations;
(2) Failing to inspect motor vehicles and examine supporting documents and vouchers in accordance with regulations;
(3) Intentionally making things difficult, delaying, or refusing to handle motor vehicle registration;
(4) Increasing motor vehicle registration conditions or required supporting documents and vouchers in violation of these Provisions;
(5) Determining motor vehicle license plate numbers by other means in violation of Article 43;
(6) Handling motor vehicle registration and related services across administrative regions in violation of regulations;
(7) Colluding with illegal intermediaries to obtain economic benefits;
(8) Exceeding authority to enter the computer registration management system to handle motor vehicle registration and related services, or failing to use the computer registration management system to handle motor vehicle registration and related services in accordance with regulations;
(9) Invading the computer registration management system in violation of regulations, leaking, altering, or trading system data, or leaking system passwords;
(10) Selling or providing motor vehicle registration information to others in violation of regulations;
(11) Participating in or indirectly participating in the business activities of motor vehicle safety technical inspection institutions;
(12) Requesting or accepting property from others or seeking other benefits by taking advantage of their position;
(13) Ordering vehicle management offices to handle motor vehicle registration in violation of these Provisions.
Traffic police who fail to use law enforcement recorders in accordance with the third paragraph of Article 73 shall be given sanctions in accordance with relevant regulations based on the severity of the circumstances.
Article 84 Where a public security organ traffic management department has any of the acts listed in Article 83, corresponding sanctions shall be given to the directly responsible person in charge and other directly responsible persons in accordance with relevant regulations.
Where a public security organ traffic management department and its staff have any of the acts listed in Article 83 and cause losses to the parties, they shall bear liability for compensation according to law.
Chapter 7 Supplementary Provisions
Article 85 The styles of motor vehicle registration certificates, license plates, vehicle licenses, and inspection qualification marks shall be uniformly formulated and supervised for production by the Ministry of Public Security.
The production of motor vehicle registration certificates, license plates, vehicle licenses, and inspection qualification marks shall comply with relevant standards.
Article 86 Motor vehicle owners may entrust agents to apply for various motor vehicle registration and related services, except for changes of joint owners, applications for replacement of motor vehicle registration certificates, and cancellation of registration due to loss of motor vehicles; where motor vehicle owners are unable to appear due to death, exit from the country, serious illness, disability, or force majeure, they may, upon presentation of relevant proof, entrust agents to apply on their behalf, or heirs may apply.
When agents apply for motor vehicle registration and related services, they shall submit the agent's identity proof and the motor vehicle owner's power of attorney.
Article 87 Public security organ traffic management departments shall implement electronic archiving of motor vehicle registration records; electronic motor vehicle archives shall have the same effect as paper archives. Vehicle management offices shall archive proof and vouchers that do not need to retain originals when handling motor vehicle registration in the form of electronic files.
Article 88 The terms "imported motor vehicles" and "import vouchers for imported motor vehicles" as used in these Provisions refer to:
(1) Imported motor vehicles:
1. Automobiles imported through customs at ports designated by the state;
2. Other motor vehicles imported through customs at various ports;
3. Motor vehicles under customs supervision;
4. Motor vehicles confiscated by law enforcement departments authorized by the state that are smuggled, lack legal import vouchers, or are illegally assembled (combined) using imported key components.
(2) Import vouchers for imported motor vehicles:
1. The import voucher for imported automobiles is the Goods Import Certificate issued by customs at state-designated ports;
2. The import voucher for other imported motor vehicles is the Goods Import Certificate issued by customs at various ports;
3. The import voucher for motor vehicles under customs supervision is the Notice for Entry/Exit and License Plate Issuance/Cancellation of Supervised Vehicles issued by the customs at the place of supervision;
4. The import voucher for motor vehicles confiscated by law enforcement departments authorized by the state that are smuggled, lack import vouchers, or are illegally assembled (combined) using imported key components is the Certificate of Confiscation of Smuggled Automobiles and Motorcycles issued by that department.
Article 89 The terms "motor vehicle owner," "identity proof," and "domicile" as used in these Provisions refer to:
(1) Motor vehicle owners include individuals or units owning motor vehicles.
1. Individuals refer to residents of mainland China and military personnel (including the Armed Police), as well as residents of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, the Macao Special Administrative Region, and the Taiwan region, Chinese citizens residing abroad, and foreigners;
2. Units refer to government organs, enterprises, public institutions, and social organizations, as well as foreign embassies and consulates in China, foreign offices in China, and representative offices of international organizations in China

structure.
（二）Identity documents:
1. Identity documents of organs, enterprises, public institutions, and social organizations are the unified social credit code certificate, business license, or social organization legal person registration certificate of such unit, as well as a power of attorney affixed with the unit's official seal and the identity document of the agent. Where the owner of a motor vehicle is an internal institution of a unit and does not meet the conditions for obtaining a unified social credit code certificate, it may use the unified social credit code certificate of the superior unit as the identity document of the motor vehicle owner. Where the aforementioned unit has been deregistered, revoked, or declared bankrupt, and its motor vehicle needs to handle change registration, transfer registration, release of mortgage registration, deregistration, release of pledge filing, or replacement or reissuance of motor vehicle registration certificate, license plate, or driving license, the identity document of the deregistered enterprise is the Notice of Approval for Deregistration issued by the market supervision and administration department; the identity document of the revoked organ, public institution, or social organization is the relevant certificate issued by its competent superior authority; for an enterprise that has gone bankrupt and has no valid business license, its identity document is the relevant certificate issued by the property liquidation institution established according to law or the bankruptcy administrator designated by the people's court according to law. Where commercial banks or automobile finance companies apply for mortgage registration business, their identity document is the business license or a copy of the business license affixed with the official seal;
2. The identity document of foreign embassies and consulates in China, foreign offices stationed in China, and representative offices of international organizations in China is the certificate issued by such embassy, consulate, office, or representative office;
3. The identity document of residents is the resident identity card or temporary resident identity card. For mainland residents living outside their place of household registration, their identity document is the resident identity card or temporary resident identity card, as well as the residence certificate or residence registration certificate issued by the public security organ;
4. The identity document of military personnel (including armed police) is the resident identity card or temporary resident identity card. Before obtaining a resident identity card, it is the valid military personnel identity document issued by the relevant military department, such as officer's certificate, civilian cadre certificate, soldier's certificate, retirement certificate, or retirement certificate, as well as the proof of personal residence issued by the unit at or above the regimental level where they serve;
5. The identity document of residents of the Hong Kong and Macao Special Administrative Regions is the residence permit for Hong Kong and Macao residents; or the Mainland Travel Permit for Hong Kong and Macao Residents they hold or the Travel Document of the People's Republic of China issued by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, as well as the accommodation registration certificate issued by the public security organ;
6. The identity document of residents of the Taiwan region is the residence permit for Taiwan residents; or the five-year valid Mainland Travel Permit for Taiwan Residents issued by the public security organ or the Travel Document of the People's Republic of China issued by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs they hold, as well as the accommodation registration certificate issued by the public security organ;
7. The identity document of Chinese citizens settled abroad is the passport of the People's Republic of China and the accommodation registration certificate issued by the public security organ;
8. The identity document of foreigners is the valid passport or other international travel document they hold, the valid visa with a stay or residence period of more than three months or the stay or residence permit, as well as the accommodation registration certificate issued by the public security organ; or the foreigner permanent residence identity card;
9. The identity document of personnel of foreign embassies and consulates in China and personnel of representative offices of international organizations in China is the valid identity document issued by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
（三）Domicile:
1. The domicile of a unit is the location of its principal office;
2. The domicile of an individual is the place of household registration or the address recorded in their identity document. The domicile of a mainland resident living outside their place of household registration is the address recorded in the residence certificate or residence registration certificate issued by the public security organ.
Where handling business other than motor vehicle registration, transfer registration, change of domicile, or change of co-owners outside the place of household registration, the motor vehicle owner is exempt from submitting the residence certificate or residence registration certificate issued by the public security organ.
Where handling registration of small and micro non-operating passenger cars outside the place of household registration, the motor vehicle owner is exempt from submitting the residence certificate or residence registration certificate issued by the public security organ.
Article 90 The term "proof of origin of motor vehicle" and "motor vehicle whole vehicle factory certificate of conformity" as used in these Provisions refers to:
（一）Proof of origin of motor vehicle:
1. For motor vehicles purchased domestically, the proof of origin is the unified invoice for motor vehicle sales or the second-hand vehicle transaction invoice. For motor vehicles purchased abroad, the proof of origin is the sales invoice issued by the sales unit of the vehicle and its translated text, but motor vehicles under customs supervision do not need to provide proof of origin;
2. For motor vehicles confiscated, recovered, or ordered to be returned by supervisory organs according to law, the proof of origin is the legal document issued by the supervisory organ, as well as the corresponding assistance in execution notice;
3. For motor vehicles transferred through mediation, ruling, or judgment by the people's court, the proof of origin is the effective mediation letter, ruling, or judgment issued by the people's court, as well as the corresponding assistance in execution notice;
4. For motor vehicles transferred through arbitration award by an arbitration institution, the proof of origin is the arbitration award and the assistance in execution notice issued by the people's court;
5. For motor vehicles involved in inheritance, gift, prize winning, agreement divorce, and agreement offset of debts, the proof of origin is the relevant documents on inheritance, gift, prize winning, agreement divorce, and agreement offset of debts, and the notarial certificate issued by the notary office;
6. For motor vehicles included in asset restructuring or overall asset sale and purchase, the proof of origin is the approval document of the asset competent department;
7. For motor vehicles uniformly purchased by organs, enterprises, public institutions, and social organizations and allocated to subordinate units without registration, the proof of origin is the unified invoice for motor vehicle sales and the allocation certificate issued by that department;
